# building_roads:
# CSES 1666, Building Roads (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1666), in our own
# words: city_count cities and some two-way roads, each between two cities; the
# fewest new roads that make every city reachable from every other. CSES also
# prints the new roads; we take their count only, since the count is what the
# problem's definition fixes. The input is the number of cities, a binary natural
# (corpora/library/binary/natural), at least 1, and the roads, a Scott list
# (corpora/library/prelude/list) of pairs `pair a b`
# (corpora/library/prelude/pair), the cities binary naturals from 1 to the
# number of cities. The answer is a binary natural. Part of the CSES port's third
# batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: city b is reachable from city a within
# steps roads when a = b, or when some road joins a to a city that reaches b within
# one step fewer (steps 0 allows no road); a city is the first of its
# component when no smaller city reaches it, within city_count steps, which
# is enough for any trip that repeats no city; the components are counted by their first cities,
# and the fewest new roads are the components minus one (each new road joins
# at most two components, and one road between two components of a chain of them
# joins them). Under tabling the reading shares the reachability for each steps and pair of
# cities, about city_count cubed times the roads; the replacement the family asks for is a union-find over the roads,
# about the roads times the inverse Ackermann function of the cities, on fixed-width integers.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application
# only: its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal. It β-reduces
# to V, the canonical binary numeral of the answer: every recursion ends, since
# reaches consumes steps, a binary numeral that falls by one at each call, the
# count and the check of the first cities consume the bounded gap city_count - city,
# and every other recursion consumes a finite list; the branches that a Scott
# boolean discards are never read. binary_subtract, which writes no top
# (../common/binary_modular), is asked for steps - 1 only when steps is not zero,
# and for the components minus one with the components at least 1, since city 1 is the first of its own component (there are
# city_count >= 1 cities). So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the soundness of the
# derivable equations for the contextual preorder of Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an
# answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W,
# while Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to
# λx y. y, and applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the
# second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ binary_odd _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment _ _ merge_binary_equality
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "cses") "common") "binary_modular")
λ _ binary_subtract _ _
. (λtuple. tuple (binary_odd binary_zero))
λ one
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ roads
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self steps from target
        . merge_binary_equality from target true
          ( ( λ any
              . steps false (λ_. any roads) λ_. any roads
            )
            ( fixpoint
              ( λ walk rest
                . rest false
                  λ road others
                  . road
                    λ left right
                    . merge_binary_equality from left (self (binary_subtract steps one false) right target) false
                      true
                      ( merge_binary_equality from right (self (binary_subtract steps one false) left target) false
                        true (walk others)
                      )
              )
            )
          )
      )
  )
λ reaches
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ city_count roads
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self city count
        . binary_less_than city_count city count
          ( self (merge_binary_increment city)
            ( ( fixpoint
                ( λ walk smaller
                  . binary_less_than smaller city
                    (reaches roads city_count smaller city false (walk (merge_binary_increment smaller)))
                    true
                ) one
              ) (merge_binary_increment count) count
            )
          )
      ) one binary_zero
  )
λ components
. (λtuple. tuple λcity_count roads. binary_subtract (components city_count roads) one false)
λ building_roads
. export building_roads
